config BR2_PACKAGE_XR829_FIRMWARE
	bool "xr829-firmware"
	help
	  The firmware the TrimUI Brick's XR829 Wi-Fi and Bluetooth chip
	  runs, which its drivers upload when the radio is switched on:
	  boot_xr829.bin, fw_xr829.bin and sdd_xr829.bin for Wi-Fi (the
	  Wi-Fi driver opens them in /lib/firmware by name), and
	  fw_xr829_bt.bin for Bluetooth. The sdd file and the Bluetooth
	  firmware are the ones for a 24 MHz crystal, the Brick's.

	  XRadio's closed binaries, with no license stated: they are not
	  part of plastron, are never committed, and come with no license
	  from us. The build takes them from a folder mounted at
	  /brick-xr829 (BRICK_XR829 in the Makefile, ~/brick-runtime/xr829
	  by default), as Creality's Sonic Pad SDK has them
	  (github.com/CrealityTech/sonic_pad_os at 7f37a7f,
	  package/firmware/linux-firmware/xr829). The build checks each
	  file against files.sha256 before installing anything.
